s been improved so it is  better than most others but I would say  that the airpods 3 are more comfortable  for my ears if I'm using them for more  than two to three hours at a time  overall I think it really depends on  your ear shape and Some people prefer  these While others would like the ear  tips especially with that new extra  small size now another reason why people  like the airpods 3 is the fact that you  still hear outside sounds because it  doesn't seal it in but the airpods pro  have the transparency mode which is now  adaptive and the microphones have been  really improved so you hear everything  just as good as these ones right here  sometimes even better and apple showed  off in loud situations that they could  actually lower that outside sound to  make sure it doesn't damage your hearing  I've only had that happen one time in  real use when my kids dropped something  and I was shocked that it didn't sound  very loud so basically the airpods Pro 2  can be used as hearing protection even  if you hear outside sounds now with that  we have the active noise cancellation  which is insanely good the third gen  airpods let all the sound in so if  you're mowing your lawn for example you  still hear all of that noise and it's  hard to hear your music and it's bad for  your ears these ones will block that out  they do an insanely good job I've never  heard of earbuds that sound anywhere  close to this good and with that I was  in my truck I started up my truck as a  V8 it has to warm up and I thought that  my truck didn't start even though the  dials moved up because it blocked out  all of that sound they do a crazy good  job but it's so convenient having that  feature now I haven't flown to the  airpods Pro 2 just yet typically I will  take my airpods Max but I did some side  by side comparisons and I was shocked by  how close they were early this morning  it was raining like crazy and I compare  them to the airpods max and I was  shocked that the high noises of the  raindrops falling were actually quieter  with the airpods Pro 2 than the airpods  max so if you're somebody that has  dedicated over ears when you fly I think  that the airpod pros 2 will do a good  enough job not to need those at all  another thing I liked about the airpods  3 was the microphone quality it was an  improvement over the original airpods  but now we have these so let's go ahead  and take a look at at three different  scenarios and compare how the  microphones do this is the microphone  quality of Apple's airpods 3 in a room  with some background HVAC noise and this  is a micron quality of Apple's airpods 2  in a regular room with some background  HVAC noise and this is the micro quality  of Apple's airpods 3 with some  background ambient noise like if you're  in a restaurant or a busy Cafe and this  isn't my phone quality of Apple's  airpods Pro 2. if you're in a busy room  or a noisy environment and this is a  micro quality of the airpods 3 if you're  in a windy environment and you have to  be talking on the phone and this is the  microphone quality of Apple's airpods  Pro 2. if you are in a windy environment  and you need to talk on the phone there  you guys go you let me know your  thoughts down in the comments section  below I think overall the airpods pro  did great other than that windy  situation where at the end they cut out  for a little bit uh but before that they  sounded wonderful I think it might be  because of the microphones along with  the new Bluetooth that's included so  with that we have the new H2 chip that  is what does all the processing we also  have Bluetooth 5.3 which has better  range it uses less power and I think  that also helps it out but another thing  that it helps with is the ability of the  case to tell your phone the battery  level without having to have the earbuds  in there to make that transmission over  Bluetooth now the airpods 2 also have  the U1 Ultra wide band chip and that  gives you Precision finding so not only  will tell you if you're somewhat close  but it will guide you to your lost  airpods and if it's in a dark room that  led will Flash and with that you have  the speaker that will make a chime so  that is actually at least a 29 value  because you're practically have an air  tag built in but with a little bit more  features if you lose a third gen airpods  it's going to be much much harder to  find them thanks to those new Chips I  also found that switching devices is  much quicker and sometimes when you try  to period airpods you'll notice that it  doesn't switch over you have to tap it  now it just works so much faster with my  new iPhone 14 pro it is really nice as  far as controls the airpods Pro 2 also  give you that swiping feature now to be  honest in the last week I've only used  it one time and that is when I did not  have my Apple watch on me so I couldn't  just Spin My Crown to adjust my volume  but for a lot of people that don't have  an Apple Watch if you're used to asking  Siri to do it that is definitely nice to  have and now we have to talk about music  quality and that is the reason why I  ditched all the extra features of the  previous pros and went with the threes  because they sounded so much better well  this time around the pros sound  incredible I was a bit bummed when they  didn't show off that it doesn't have  dual drivers like Samsung's but when I  heard them for myself it is shocking how  good it is the airpods Pro 2 play as low  as 20 Hertz and they play it Loud the  airpods Pro 3 can play it but much much  quieter and these can actually play 15  Hertz like in this test track here where  you actually hear that and you feel that  and with the airpods 3 you don't hear  any of those low notes now with that  even though these are sealed The Sound  Stage is quite a bit better spatial  audio works better especially once you  optimize it and pretty much every track  that I listen to is better in every  single way it also plays louder without  Distortion and the separation between  instruments especially in heavy songs we  have a lot of tracks like rock music is  definitely better as well so if you have  these because you like the sound quality  I mean the airpods Pro 2 are on a whole  nother level so with all of that said If  you're trying to decide which one to buy  I would say that if you can afford to  spend 250 bucks or if they're discounted  I'll have a link down below you guys  could check the current price I would  pay the extra money compared to getting  a discounted pair of these is even for  the fact that you can find them if you  lose them and all those other benefits  it is just an amazing pair of earbuds  you guys let me know your thoughts down  below below click that Circle above to  subscribe check out one of those great  videos right over there this has been  Max and I'll see you in the next video  [Music]
 

